/-!
# Places over j = 1728, 0, ∞ with bounded order

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.LevelN.exists_place_ord_jGen_le_two_three_level`
(`22403f45-52e1-540f-9ffe-50574b348b25`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `e9c18715-395e-5fd7-9ece-36af95baa797`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and let $A_N$ denote [`ModularCurve.LevelN.ring
N`](def/ModularCurve_LevelNFunctionField.html#L28), the $\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra of the algebra of
functions $\mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ generated by the function $j = E_4^3/\Delta$ (`jAnalytic`)
together with all Fricke functions `fricke N v` for nonzero $v \in (\mathbb{Z}/N)^2$. Let $K$ be a
field carrying a $\mathbb{C}$-algebra structure and an $A_N$-algebra structure, compatible as a
scalar tower over $\mathbb{C}$, and such that $K$ is a fraction field of $A_N$. Write $j$ also for
the image in $K$ of the element `jGen N` of $A_N$ given by $E_4^3/\Delta$. Here a place of $K$ over
$\mathbb{C}$ is a valuation subring of $K$ containing the image of $\mathbb{C}$, distinct from all
of $K$, and a principal ideal ring; its function $\operatorname{ord}$ is the associated normalised
additive valuation with values in $\mathbb{Z}$. The assertion is the conjunction of three existence
statements: there is a place $W$ with $0 < \operatorname{ord}_W(j - 1728) \le 2$; there is a place
$W$ with $0 < \operatorname{ord}_W(j) \le 3$; and there is a place $W$ with $\operatorname{ord}_W(j)
< 0$ and $-N \le \operatorname{ord}_W(j)$.

This records, in the language of places of the function field of the modular curve of level $N$ over
$\mathbb{C}$, that the map $j$ has a point over $j = 1728$ of ramification index at most $2$, a
point over $j = 0$ of ramification index at most $3$, and a pole of order at most $N$ over the cusp;
the three places arise from $\tau = i$, $\tau = e^{2\pi i/3}$ and the cusp $i\infty$ in the
parameter $q_N$. It is used in the degree and ramification estimates for the coverings of modular
curves, in particular in bounding double cosets by fibres and in the computation of ramification
indices along the inclusions of $\Gamma_0$- and $\Gamma_H$-level structures.

